    "reading": "# Positioning · JubAp.Net’s GEPLAN Case before SaaS and IoT Revolutions\nSource document: https://jubap.net/engineering-value-creation-before-the-cloud-jubap-nets-geplan-case-before-saas-and-iot-revolutions\n\n## JubAp.Net’s GEPLAN Case before SaaS and IoT Revolutions\nJubAp.Net, the organisation behind the GEPLAN suite, operates today as a complex-systems intelligence centre specialising in Operational AI Integrity and early-warning regime-change detection. Its roots trace back to the early 2000s — to an integrated operational platform built long before public cloud, commercial IoT or plug-and-play APIs existed.\n\nIts roots trace back to the early 2000s, when the practice operated through The Integral Management Society in the United States and Corbera Networks in Mexico. Built from a Nokia R&D engineering background and later grounded in Veracruz, the team developed mission-critical systems for logistics-intensive environments such as PEMEX, TETSA and regional transport operators.\n\nGEPLAN was not conceived as a conventional software product. It was engineered as an integrated operational platform: a system capable of connecting logistics, maintenance, inventory, procurement, telemetry, volumetric control and operational estimation inside a single execution environment.\nTags: Regime changes and early warning 31.25%; Business and management 18.75%; Mobility and infrastructure 43.75%; Transformation and operational continuity 6.25%\nCard: https://dakleyer.github.io/perspective-beyond/sources/jubap-nets-geplan-case-before-saas-and-iot-revolutions-n1265/\nSource document: https://jubap.net/engineering-value-creation-before-the-cloud-jubap-nets-geplan-case-before-saas-and-iot-revolutions/\n\n## Observabilidad del proceso\nReconstruct work, events and dependencies from observable evidence.\nTags: Agents and distributed coordination 0.39%; Learning and capability transmission 3.42%; Authority, permissions and delegation 1.20%; Human capability and intelligence debt 5.10%; Use cases and applications 3.16%; Minimum control and sufficiency 8.11%; Decisions and responsibility 9.88%; Research and technical documentation 3.94%; Economics, costs and liquidity 8.65%; Business and management 15.15%; Standards and interoperability 1.68%; Evidence, provenance and attribution 8.58%; Experimentation, falsification and counterexamples 2.62%; AI integrity and security 0.40%; Memory, community and territory 2.89%; Mobility and infrastructure 10.92%; Change of perspective 1.64%; Representation and formal boundaries 2.74%; Transformation and operational continuity 9.53%\nCard: https://dakleyer.github.io/perspective-beyond/concepts/process-observability/\n\n## Capacidad reutilizable\nA useful function can sometimes outlive the tool or channel where it first appeared.\nTags: Agents and distributed coordination 1.41%; Learning and capability transmission 2.96%; Authority, permissions and delegation 1.30%; Regime changes and early warning 1.90%; Human capability and intelligence debt 7.90%; Use cases and applications 4.40%; Minimum control and sufficiency 2.01%; Decisions and responsibility 5.93%; Research and technical documentation 6.97%; Economics, costs and liquidity 3.30%; Business and management 17.72%; Standards and interoperability 0.64%; Evidence, provenance and attribution 9.71%; Experimentation, falsification and counterexamples 1.81%; Geopolitics and borders 1.60%; AI integrity and security 3.15%; Memory, community and territory 4.94%; Mobility and infrastructure 10.70%; Representation and formal boundaries 0.60%; Transformation and operational continuity 11.05%\nCard: https://dakleyer.github.io/perspective-beyond/concepts/reusable-capability/\n\n## Traducción de captura a arquitectura\nTranslate observations into value chains, capabilities, critical paths and competencies before process modelling.\nTags: Agents and distributed coordination 3.27%; Learning and capability transmission 2.47%; Authority, permissions and delegation 2.22%; Human capability and intelligence debt 3.25%; Cartography and ecosystem signals 3.27%; Use cases and applications 0.54%; Minimum control and sufficiency 0.93%; Decisions and responsibility 4.17%; Research and technical documentation 3.08%; Economics, costs and liquidity 4.52%; Business and management 12.19%; Standards and interoperability 3.56%; Evidence, provenance and attribution 26.55%; Experimentation, falsification and counterexamples 0.89%; AI integrity and security 3.27%; Mathematics 0.85%; Memory, community and territory 1.16%; Mobility and infrastructure 1.54%; Open world and indeterminacy 9.40%; Representation and formal boundaries 1.54%; Transformation and operational continuity 11.33%\nCard: https://dakleyer.github.io/perspective-beyond/concepts/from-capture-to-architecture/\n\n## Migración y capitalización de capacidad\nCapability creation, carriers, operation and value capture can occur in different places.\nTags: Learning and capability transmission 0.64%; Authority, permissions and delegation 0.63%; Human capability and intelligence debt 8.39%; Use cases and applications 4.69%; Minimum control and sufficiency 1.34%; Decisions and responsibility 7.09%; Economics, costs and liquidity 16.16%; Business and management 15.66%; Evidence, provenance and attribution 20.84%; Experimentation, falsification and counterexamples 2.86%; Memory, community and territory 7.73%; Mobility and infrastructure 2.86%; Transformation and operational continuity 11.11%\nCard: https://dakleyer.github.io/perspective-beyond/concepts/capability-migration-and-value-capture/\n\nGEPLAN – Inteligencia Logística para Entornos Críticos de PEMEX 2006- → JubAp.Net’s GEPLAN Case before SaaS and IoT Revolutions · analogy only. The pre-SaaS note can connect modular delivery with the reported operating-value loop, while keeping released resources distinct from independently verified net returns.\n\n## GEPLAN – Inteligencia Logística para Entornos Críticos de PEMEX 2006-\n\nTags: Evidence, provenance and attribution 28.57%; Mobility and infrastructure 71.43%\nCard: https://dakleyer.github.io/perspective-beyond/sources/geplan-inteligencia-logistica-para-entornos-criticos-de-pemex-2006-l008/\nSource document: https://www.latinoempresa.com/post/tegrity-ai-caso-de-estudio-geplan-inteligencia-logística-para-entornos-críticos-de-pemex-2006\n\nJubAp.Net’s GEPLAN Case before SaaS and IoT Revolutions → Comparación justa · documenta el concepto. \n\n## Comparación justa\nCompare alternatives under equivalent obligations, information access and budgets.\nTags: Agents and distributed coordination 3.25%; Learning and capability transmission 1.27%; Authority, permissions and delegation 0.84%; Regime changes and early warning 2.23%; Human capability and intelligence debt 2.93%; Use cases and applications 3.42%; Minimum control and sufficiency 2.87%; Decisions and responsibility 4.12%; Research and technical documentation 17.02%; Economics, costs and liquidity 13.01%; Business and management 2.04%; Evidence, provenance and attribution 8.04%; Experimentation, falsification and counterexamples 13.73%; Mathematics 1.70%; Memory, community and territory 1.70%; Mobility and infrastructure 21.38%; Transformation and operational continuity 0.45%\nCard: https://dakleyer.github.io/perspective-beyond/concepts/matched-comparison/\n\nCar Evolution Mobility OS – Competition → Comparación justa · documenta el concepto. \n\n## Car Evolution Mobility OS – Competition\n\nTags: Mobility and infrastructure 100.00%\nCard: https://dakleyer.github.io/perspective-beyond/sources/car-evolution-mobility-os-competition-e1956/\nSource document: https://jubap.eu/mobility/competition/\n\n"
